     The beacon Driftwire hears nearby (docs/design/28 "Finding each other",
     src/addons/driftwire/wire.h), for firewall-cmd's add-service option. It
     arrives to the group 239.255.77.83 and to the subnet broadcast, so the
     service names no destination. The transfer's own TCP connection is on a
     port the receiver's system picks, so no service can name it (driftwire(1),
     FIREWALL). -->
<service>
  <short>Driftwire</short>
  <description>Lets this computer hear the Driftwire beacons of computers nearby (UDP 47613), so driftwire and MediaViewer's Driftwire add-on list them. Receiving nearby also needs incoming TCP from the local network, on a port the system picks.</description>
  <port protocol="udp" port="47613"/>
</service>
